## Delivered

Frozen contract: src/ClientIntake/ with 51 exported types across Models,
Contracts, and Services. Every workflow constructor and method throws
NotImplementedException; the module implements none of its own ports; nothing in
the portal references, registers, resolves, or invokes it. IIntakeStore has
exactly two firm-omitting members, both keyed-digest lookups returning trusted
scope. IIntakeContentStore exposes no read member.

Blazor foundation: App, Routes, PortalLayout, ReviewPage. No component declares
@rendermode or @page; no global render mode is applied; static SSR is the
default. ReviewEndpoints.cs returns RazorComponentResult<ReviewPage> with one
closed ReviewPageModel, and retains its route, policy, headers, trusted-firm
extraction, browser-safety guard, closed projection, invariant amounts,
collection order, single FindAsync call with the request cancellation token, and
identical empty 404.

## Human-directed amendments, applied before merge

1. STATIC SSR ONLY — Interactive Server moved to T03.
   Removed AddInteractiveServerComponents() and AddInteractiveServerRenderMode(),
   and the blazor.web.js reference in App.razor. No T01 component declares an
   interactive render mode, so the registration provided no current functionality
   while materializing four /_blazor SignalR endpoints on the taxpayer-data host.
   Kept: AddRazorComponents(), MapRazorComponents<App>(), the typed
   RazorComponentResult review rendering, and all endpoint-owned authorization
   and safe-404 behaviour.

   Endpoint surface before -> after: 12 route endpoints -> 8. The four /_blazor
   endpoints are gone; /_framework/opaque-redirect remains, contributed by
   MapRazorComponents itself and taking no route parameter. Asserted by
   ShellPageTests.NoInteractiveServerCircuitEndpointIsMapped, by an exact
   production-source scan for every interactive-registration token, and by
   PortalBoundaryTests.TheHostShipsNoClientScriptReference.

   Wording updated in architecture.md (marked [AMENDED]), tasks.md T01
   requirement 5 and T03 requirement 8 (marked [AMENDED]), root CLAUDE.md,
   README.md, NEXT.md, and src/TaxAI.Portal/CLAUDE.md.

2. IIntakeSecretSource -> IIntakeCredentialSource (type and file).
   The repository forbids any tracked file name containing "secret" — a hygiene
   guard against committed secret material, enforced independently by
   TaxCases.Tests.RepositoryHygiene_HasNoForbiddenTrackedFiles and
   DocumentExtraction.Tests.NoForbiddenFileIsTrackedAnywhereInTheRepository.
   src/ClientIntake/Contracts/IIntakeSecretSource.cs tripped it.

   The guard was NOT weakened. The port and its file were renamed instead, on the
   human's decision. Every method signature on the port is identical, and the
   secret-bearing value type IntakeSecret is unchanged. The constructor parameter
   was renamed secretSource -> credentialSource for coherence.

   This surfaced only after the first commit: the hygiene tests scan
   `git ls-files`, so the file was invisible to them while untracked. The earlier
   green gate was testing a genuinely different state, not a wrong one.

