src/TaxLogicEngine; no EF migration; no model snapshot; no schema artifact; no
persisted or review public contract.

## Scope exceptions — two files outside T01's owned list

1. tests/TaxAI.Portal.Tests/Upgrade/DotNet10RepositoryTests.cs
   Spec 013 shipped a closed-set assertion over every project in TaxAI.sln,
   which the root CLAUDE.md forbids. It blocked this task's required solution
   additions outright. Replaced with per-project presence-and-uniqueness; the two
   ClientIntake paths added to ApprovedProjects; every other assertion in the
   file untouched. EXPLICITLY AUTHORIZED BY THE HUMAN before implementation
   began, after the blocker was reported with options.

2. scripts/Assert-DotNet10Toolchain.ps1
   The same defect in the executable preflight. Fixed additively: the two
   ClientIntake paths were added to the $approvedProjects registry. No assertion
   weakened; the set stays closed and still rejects any unregistered project.
   Discovered only when the gate ran, after the authorization above.

Both are recorded in PR #133 for the reviewer.

