## Known, reported, not fixed

- One flaky run of TaxAI.Portal.Tests.Identity.CookieAndTokenTests
  .TheDecryptedCookieCarriesNoFirmNoUserAndNoTaxpayerValue was observed once and
  did not reproduce in five subsequent full runs. It is a pre-existing identity /
  Data-Protection test that touches neither the component model nor routing.
  Reported rather than suppressed; worth watching in CI.
- dotnet publish materializes the framework's own wwwroot/_framework/
  blazor.web.js and blazor.server.js. They ship with the shared framework's
  static web assets, no component references them, and nothing loads them. The
  repository's own wwwroot contains exactly portal.css.

## Deliberately not shipped

No intake route, workflow body, relational intake table, or encrypted content
adapter. No interactive component, no Interactive Server registration, no
/_blazor endpoint, and no client script. Deployment refusal unchanged:
Development-only startup, and no deployment anywhere that can receive real
taxpayer data.

## Human review required

Not merged. Not self-approved. T02 must not begin until this marker is on
master.
